(TM) i7-8700K CPU @ 3.70GHz (12 threads) - 31.26 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the mouse is captured on Firefox in a HTML5 export, the mouse moves significantly slower than any other platform and even compared to when it is not captured it is much slower. This cannot be observed in Chrome.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a new project (call it something like mouse test)\n- Create a 2D Scene\n- Add a sprite with the icon.svg texture\n\n- Copy and Paste this script into the Icon Sprite\n```gdscript\nextends Sprite2D\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tDisplayServer.warp_mouse(Vector2i(1280 / 2, 720 /2))\n\nfunc _input(event: InputEvent) -> void:\n\tif event is InputEventMouseMotion:\n\t\tposition.x += event.relative.x * 1\n\t\tposition.y += event.relative.y * 1\n\telif event is InputEventMouseButton:\n\t\tInput.set_mouse_mode(Input.MOUSE_MODE_CAPTURED)\n```\n\n- Remote Deploy to HTML5\n- Test Speed uncaptured\n- Test Speed when captured\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[108856.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/21583761/108856.zip)\n\n_Production edit: added MRP, and reproducible in 4.4.1 and 4.3_","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108856/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108856/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}